+---
+id: task-003-fix-cancelled-coupon-reuse-and-50-free-shipping
+type: task
+title: "Fix cancelled coupon reuse and €50 free shipping"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+Investigate Paolo's rejected corrected order and the report of a €4.90 delivery fee on exactly
+€50.00 of discounted goods.
+
+The coupon defect was that redemption records the order ID, but cancellation attempted to return
+the coupon using the customer name. Cancellation now supplies the order ID, so a cancelled
+single-use welcome coupon becomes redeemable again. A red-first regression test places Paolo's
+order, cancels it on the same day, and confirms the corrected order can redeem the same code.
+
+The existing delivery implementation compares the discounted, pre-VAT goods total inclusively
+against €50.00. Its existing exact-boundary test confirms that €5,000 cents receives free delivery;
+this criterion was characterized as already passing, so no delivery logic changed.
+
+Verification: the new coupon test failed before the fix because `WELCOME` remained associated with
+`ORD-0001`. After the fix, all 24 tests pass with `npm test`; `git diff --check` also passes. No
+new dependencies were introduced.
